# GAIA

Sustainability metrics platform. Three repos: `gaia-api` (Django), `gaia-web` (Next.js), `GAIA` (orchestration).

## Agent Routing

All agents in `.opencode/agents/` (single source of truth).

### Orchestrators (top-level)

| Agent | Role |
|-------|------|
| `senior-backend` | Backend orchestrator — delegates to sub-agents in parallel |
| `sustainability-specialist` | Domain authority — LCA, RothC, regenerative metrics |
| `senior-nextjs` | Next.js frontend — shadcn/ui, TanStack Query |
| `cross-stack` | API↔Next.js contracts (OpenAPI → @hey-api/openapi-ts) |
| `software-architecture` | Architecture audit, code quality scoring |

### Backend sub-agents (dispatched by senior-backend)

| Sub-Agent | Layer | When |
|-----------|-------|------|
| `model-agent` | Models | Schema, soft-delete |
| `service-agent` | Services | Business logic, LCA/RothC |
| `selector-agent` | Selectors | Read-only queries |
| `serializer-agent` | Serializers | Schema fields, validation, OpenAPI |
| `migration-agent` | Migrations | Safe migrations, seeds |
| `test-agent` | Tests | Tests per app |
| `lint-agent` | Lint | pre-commit, ruff |

## Knowledge

- Vault: `docs/vault/00-INDEX.md`
- References: `docs/references/README.md`
- Skills: `.agents/skills/` (codegraph, ui-ux-pro-max, business-product-strategist, xlsx)

## Critical Rules

1. CodeGraph first — `codegraph_context` before grep/glob
2. Contract-first — OpenAPI schema before frontend
3. PT (UX/domain), EN (code)
4. NEVER commit without authorization
5. Views never query, services never return QuerySets
6. After API/Web source changes, run `.opencode/bin/codegraph-global-sync.sh` before the final response; the agent owns reindexing, not the developer
